+
 private:
+    // Parallel rasterization: primitives are queued and drawn by worker
+    // threads that each own interleaved 8-row bands of every target, in
+    // submission order, so every pixel sees the same operations as before.
+    // The queue is drained before anything that reads or changes VRAM or
+    // transfer state, and when a primitive would read memory an earlier
+    // queued one writes (or write memory it reads, or alias another target).
+    struct PendingPrimitive
+    {
