+        // Upscaled: the window shows the GPU's picture, so the displayed
+        // buffer is not copied back to local memory (that waited for the GPU
+        // every frame). It still is when something reads it, or when the
+        // upscaled picture can't be used and the native one is shown.
+        if (gl && !upscaled)
+            syncDisplayed();
